DGR-10: dgraphGatherAll2() error path: NULL dereference on non-roots, uninitialised free on root
=================================================================================================
Harness: ../common (gatherfi; the plain libraries are built with -ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern
so that uninitialised locals are deterministic garbage).

Pristine:
  ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/gatherfi 2 1 0 0 -- gather 0 5
  nth=0 exit=139 :: (1): ERROR: dgraphGatherAll2: out of memory (3);
                    dgraph_gather_all.c:212:16: runtime error: member access within null pointer of type 'struct Graph'
  ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/gatherfi 2 0 0 3 -- gather 0 5
  nth=0 exit=139 :: (0): ERROR: dgraphGatherAll2: out of memory (1); signal 11  <- free(recvcnttab), uninitialised
  nth=1 exit=139 :: (0): ERROR: dgraphGatherAll2: out of memory (2); signal 11  <- same
  nth=2 exit=1   :: rank 0 rc=1, rank 1 rc=0 (no agreement, PS-DGR-4)

Patched (commit 0004): non-root nth=0 and root nth=0..2: exit=1, both ranks "gather rc=1";
  nth=3: rc=0 and the centralized graph checks; alias mode (API-04) unchanged.

Twin hdgraphGather() (same commit), through SCOTCH_dgraphOrderCompute (orderfi, m16x16.grf, np=4),
allocation #123 on rank 0 is "hdgraphGather: out of memory (2)":
  pristine: ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/orderfi 4 0 123 123 -- data/m16x16.grf
            exit=139, signal 11: hgraphExit() frees a never-set edge array with a never-set base value
  patched:  exit=1, no crash, ranks 0,1 "cannot compute ordering".
  (ranks 2,3 return 0 in both cases: the two folded halves of hdgraphOrderNd2() do not agree on
  failure in release builds, hdgraph_order_nd.c:301-307, another group's file; see extra.json.)

Correction (review round 2): the signal 11 at root nth=0,1 ("free(recvcnttab), uninitialised") occurs only in
the kit's -ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern build. In a plain -O1 build of pristine 7.0.18 the same runs return
rc=1 on rank 0 and rc=0 on rank 1 without crashing (the uninitialised free is still undefined behaviour).
The non-root nth=0 NULL dereference (signal 11) reproduces in both builds.
